{"nodes": [{"id": "recovered_prediction_onefunc_session_28_prediction_onefunc_s28", "label": "PREDICTION-ONEFUNC (session 28): both standing correlation forms combined into one mathematical function", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-ONEFUNC-SESSION-28.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "M ruled: do not state both forms \u2014 combine them into ONE mathematical function, so the law has no choice in it."}, {"id": "recovered_prediction_onefunc_session_28_one_correlation_function_e_c_of_f", "label": "E_c(f) := E_c[n_c + f n_e] - f E_c^pol[f n_e] - (f-independent SIC of other shells)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-ONEFUNC-SESSION-28.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Both standing forms are functionals of this one function: the midpoint form is E_c'(1/2) and the integer form is E_c(1) - E_c(0), recovered as truncations of one expression rather than as alternatives."}, {"id": "recovered_prediction_onefunc_session_28_gap_as_derived_curvature", "label": "GAP := [E_c(1)-E_c(0)] - E_c'(1/2) = (1/24)E_c'''(xi), a derived curvature in the occupation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-ONEFUNC-SESSION-28.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The midpoint is one-point Gauss quadrature of the exact integral, exact iff E_c is quadratic in f; so the gap is curvature by derivation and the law's term is midpoint plus its curvature completion."}, {"id": "recovered_prediction_onefunc_session_28_f2_ln_f_sic_correlation_law", "label": "Closed form: the SIC piece carries +(lam0(1)/3) N_e^- f^2 ln f, contributing +0.00100 N_e^- Ha to GAP", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-ONEFUNC-SESSION-28.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The correlation analogue of the f^(4/3) exchange law found in session 25; closed form, so it can be checked rather than fitted."}, {"id": "recovered_prediction_onefunc_session_28_failure_mode_of_the_whole_idea", "label": "Stated failure mode: if the integral is not captured by three slopes the gap is not curvature of E_c(f) and 'one function' is insufficient", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-ONEFUNC-SESSION-28.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Report, do not tune; no scan in f beyond the five fixed points and no new orbitals."}], "edges": [{"source": "recovered_prediction_onefunc_session_28_prediction_onefunc_s28", "target": "recovered_prediction_onefunc_session_28_one_correlation_function_e_c_of_f", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-ONEFUNC-SESSION-28.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recovered_prediction_onefunc_session_28_gap_as_derived_curvature", "target": "recovered_prediction_onefunc_session_28_one_correlation_function_e_c_of_f", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-ONEFUNC-SESSION-28.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recovered_prediction_onefunc_session_28_f2_ln_f_sic_correlation_law", "target": "recovered_prediction_onefunc_session_28_one_correlation_function_e_c_of_f", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-ONEFUNC-SESSION-28.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recovered_prediction_onefunc_session_28_prediction_onefunc_s28", "target": "recovered_prediction_onefunc_session_28_failure_mode_of_the_whole_idea", "relation": "references", "confidence": 